# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here so you can read
# what the registry will serve.  The registry gets its own copy, which
# `novo pkg publish` uploads beside the archive.  The page is generated
# from the sources, so committing it would be committing a second
# original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary, which `novo pkg build` names after the
# package.  A library builds none, so the line is here for when this
# package grows a `main`.
/libduckdb-sys

# Not novo.lock.  A locked build resolves the same closure twice, and
# it does so offline once the cache is warm.  A consumer never reads a
# dependency's lock, because they resolve their own closure and write
# their own.  Committing it therefore costs nobody anything and makes
# this repository's CI reproducible.  It is not on the publish
# allow-list, so it never ships either way.
